{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_016FPhanacPLShFvxXLk3sxF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Wrote **`answers/06-015-supervised-vs-unsupervised-learning.md`** covering:\n\n- **Concept:** Supervised (labeled pairs, f(x)→y) vs unsupervised (unlabeled, structure discovery) — distinguished by label presence and cost\n- **Mechanism:** Supervised loss (cross-entropy/MSE/ranking) + clean eval (AUC/F1) vs unsupervised clustering/dimensionality-reduction + harder eval (silhouette, downstream task); self-supervised as the key bridge — LLM pre-training (next-token prediction) requires no human labels\n- **Production example:** Support routing uses supervised XGBoost intent classifier; UMAP+HDBSCAN discovers emergent ticket clusters; sentence-transformer backbone pre-trained with self-supervised SimCSE\n- **Key pitfalls:** Not calling LLM pre-training \"self-supervised\" (it's not vanilla unsupervised); ignoring unsupervised eval difficulty; conflating semi-supervised with unsupervised\n\nNext up: **Q16 — Regularization: L1, L2, dropout**."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":358,"cache_read_input_tokens":69750,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":358,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0c24e4d1-fe0d-4c35-b729-8a4a85e5ae46","uuid":"c62b889b-68d5-4319-bf6c-d20328626c8a"}
